# ====================================================================
# UniEvents — .gitignore
# Author: Teodor Duracoski 223131
# ====================================================================

# --- Environment variables and secrets -----------------------------
# The config/ folder and .env files hold database URLs, API keys,
# JWT secrets, SMTP credentials for the confirmation emails, and
# similar sensitive values. They must never enter version control:
# anything pushed to Bitbucket would be permanently exposed to
# everyone with repo access (and to history forever, even if later
# deleted). Each developer keeps a local .env; production secrets
# live in a secrets manager.
config/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Compiled output and dependency folders ------------------------
# node_modules/ holds installed npm packages — gigabytes of code that
# `npm install` recreates from package.json. __pycache__/ holds
# Python bytecode regenerated on every run. dist/ and build/ hold
# bundler output (webpack, vite, tsc) that should be produced by CI
# from source, not committed. Versioning them bloats the repo and
# creates merge conflicts on every build.
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
dist/
build/
.next/
.cache/

# --- Log files -----------------------------------------------------
# Application and tooling logs (npm-debug.log, server.log, etc.) are
# runtime artifacts: noisy, machine-specific, and often contain
# request data or stack traces that may leak sensitive information.
# They have no value in version control.
*.log
logs/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# --- OS and editor cruft -------------------------------------------
# Files generated by macOS Finder, Windows Explorer, JetBrains IDEs,
# VS Code, etc. They're personal to each developer and add noise to
# diffs.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
